+---
+name: write-paths-pr964
+description: B.1–B.6 write-path convergence: both match writers produce identical 21-column rows
+metadata:
+  type: project
+---
+
+Both match write paths (compute-matches.ts and persist-session-matches.ts) must write the same 21-column field set so a match renders identically regardless of which path saved it.
+
+**Why:** Before PR #964, compute-matches.ts was missing fit_percent, fit_breakdown, cargo_item_index, vessel_item_index, worksheet_json, breakeven_tce_usd_per_day. This caused NaN%-bars and empty worksheets for pre-computed matches.
+
+**How to apply:** Any future write path must pass all 21 columns to createMatch. The parity test in lib/matching/__tests__/write-path-parity.test.ts guards this.
+
+Key changes made:
+- B.1: real-matches.ts reason_structured = null (was FitBreakdown JSON → NaN%-bars)
+- B.2: compute-matches.ts now writes fit_percent/fit_breakdown/indices/worksheet/breakeven
+- B.3: session-buckets.ts reads m.economics (canonical) instead of flat-$600 estimate
+- B.4/B.5: seed-all.ts is now 6 steps, step 5 = regen; npm run seed:regen added
+- B.6: createMatch gets refreshComputed flag (persist-session-matches only) — updates live economics on stale rows without touching status/created_at
